%N A397120 Size of Type A Megastars of star triples in the Spectre aperiodic monotile tiling.
%C A397120 The chiral aperiodic Spectre monotile tiling (discovered in 2023) forms hierarchical, fractal macro-structures called clusters of star triples (three Spectre tiles head-on) of five different families, megastars of two types, and palindromes of megastars (see A400812). This sequence gives the number of star triples in successive generations of Type A megastars.
%C A397120 A Type A megastar consists of a major star triple in the center and three arms, each a cluster of star triples of Family A (A397115) of the previous generation; each such cluster is a chain of Type C megastars (A400810).
%C A397120 The fractal growth is governed by the limiting constant 5.674473356937... = 1 + 2*sqrt(6)*cos((1/3)*arccos(sqrt(6)/4)), the largest root of x^3 - 3*x^2 - 15*x - 1 = 0, as for the Type C megastars (A400810) and the Type A palindromes (A400811).
%C A397120 The vertex span of the Type A megastar of generation n (the number of star triples on a longest path through it) is Fibonacci(3*n-2) = A033887(n-1).
%H A397120 Georg Fischer, <a href="/A397120/b397120.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100</a>
%H A397120 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="https://zenodo.org/records/18421797">Anatomy of the Spectre Tiling</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A397120 David Smith, J. S. Myers, C. S. Kaplan, and C. Goodman-Strauss, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17743">A chiral aperiodic monotile</a>, arXiv:2305.17743 [math.CO], 2023-2024.
%H A397120 <a href="/index/Rec#order_03">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,15,1).
%H A397120 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A397120/a397120.png">Type A megastar of generation 4 (73 major and 63 minor star triples)</a>
%H A397120 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A397120/a397120_1.png">Type A megastar of generation 4 with a longest path (vertex span 55 = Fibonacci(10))</a>
%H A397120 Boris K. Horvat, <a href="/A397120/a397120_2.png">All Type A megastars in the level-6 supertile</a>
%F A397120 a(n) = 3*a(n-1) + 15*a(n-2) + a(n-3) (for n>3, where a(1)=1, a(2)=4, a(3)=25).
%F A397120 a(n) = a(n-1) + 3*A400810(n-1) for n > 1.
%F A397120 a(n) = 1 + 3*A397115(n-1) for n > 1.
%F A397120 a(n) = c_1*r_1^n + c_2*r_2^n + c_3*r_3^n, where r_1, r_2, r_3 are the roots of x^3 - 3*x^2 - 15*x - 1 = 0.
%F A397120 G.f.: x*(1 - x)*(1 + 2*x)/(1 - 3*x - 15*x^2 - x^3). - _Stefano Spezia_, Jun 27 2026
%e A397120 For n = 1, the Type A megastar is a single major star triple: a(1) = 1.
%e A397120 For n = 2, it consists of the previous megastar a(1) = 1 and three Type C megastars of size A400810(1) = 1, giving 1 + 3*1 = 4 star triples.
%e A397120 For n = 3, it consists of a(2) = 4 and three Type C megastars of size A400810(2) = 7, giving 4 + 3*7 = 25 star triples.
%t A397120 LinearRecurrence[{3, 15, 1}, {1, 4, 25}, 24] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Jun 27 2026 *)
%o A397120 (PARI) Vec(x*(1 + x - 2*x^2)/(1 - 3*x - 15*x^2 - x^3) + O(x^24))
%Y A397120 Cf. A397115 (Family A), A397116 (Family C), A397117 (Family B), A397118 (Family D), A397119 (Family E).
%Y A397120 Cf. A400810 (Type C megastars), A400811 (Type A palindromes), A400812 (all star triples), A400820 (star triples in all Type A megastars).
%Y A397120 Cf. A033887, A076765.
